  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Equation of auxiliary circle is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0005_1151e8adc031.png\" style=\"width: 288px; height: 230px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Equation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>M</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>On solving Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math> sq units</p><p>Hence, option (d) is correct.</p>"
  }
